<title>CYPRUS: Cyprus nurses strike over poor staffing levels.</title>
<headline>Cyprus nurses strike over poor staffing levels.</headline>
<dateline>NICOSIA 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Around 2,000 nurses in Cyprus staged a two-hour stoppage on Thursday to press for better staffing levels in the island's hospitals.</p>
<p>The nurses, working at two state-run hospitals in the capital Nicosia and two more in the southern coastal towns of Paralimni and Larnaca, want the Health Ministry to recruit more nurses and auxiliary staff, union representatives said.</p>
<p>Nurses at state hospitals in other towns plan a two-hour stoppage next Monday if their demands are not met.</p>
</text>
